  ('299392107805911624', 'Los Angeles Plays Itself', 2004, 'Documentary', 'Thom Andersen, Deborah Stratman', 'Thom Andersen', 'Encke King, Ben Alexander, Jim Backus, Brenda Bakke, Barbara O. Jones, Gene Barry, Richard Basehart, Hugh Beaumont', null, 'From its distinctive neighborhoods to its architectural homes, Los Angeles has been the backdrop to countless movies. In this dazzling work, Andersen takes viewers on a whirlwind tour through the metropolis'' real and cinematic history, investigating the myriad stories and legends that have come to define it, and meticulously, judiciously revealing the real city that lives beneath.', 'From its distinctive neighborhoods to its architectural homes, Los Angeles has been the backdrop to countless movies. In this dazzling work, Andersen takes viewers on a whirlwind tour through the metropolis'' real and cinematic history, investigating the myriad stories and legends that have come to define it, and meticulously, judiciously revealing the real city that lives beneath.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/wmzGSQktsLf2JvfkhBaLSdG4G3Z.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:38643'),
  ('1113925869728964055', 'Los Angeles Streetfighter', 1985, 'Action', 'Richard Park Wu-sang', 'Hong Ji-wun', 'Chong Jun, Phillip Rhee, James Lew, Rosanna King, Bill Wallace, Ken Nagayama, Frank Marmolejo, Dorin Mukama', 'NR', 'Tony, the new kid at school, befriends gang leader Young, whose top rival is Chan. When Young defeats Chan in battle, two mysterious men offer Tony and Young jobs at a security agency, with one of their new clients being among the city''s most notorious drug dealers.', 'Tony, the new kid at school, befriends gang leader Young, whose top rival is Chan. When Young defeats Chan in battle, two mysterious men offer Tony and Young jobs at a security agency, with one of their new clients being among the city''s most notorious drug dealers.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3k1hKBsExunkCQawC5q3y1EmStL.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:54855'),
