  ('708211780936361848', 'Lost Course', 2021, 'Documentary', 'Jill Li', null, null, null, 'Lost Course chronicles a grassroots democratic movement in the southern Chinese village of Wukan. The villagers protest against the corrupt local officials before ousting them and organising elections of their own. However, after taking control of their destiny, the villagers find themselves beset by the same corruption and cynicism endemic. Following three main characters, Li reveals the complexities of their struggles, triumphs and setbacks from the inside.', 'Lost Course chronicles a grassroots democratic movement in the southern Chinese village of Wukan. The villagers protest against the corrupt local officials before ousting them and organising elections of their own. However, after taking control of their destiny, the villagers find themselves beset by the same corruption and cynicism endemic. Following three main characters, Li reveals the complexities of their struggles, triumphs and setbacks from the inside.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/7zOlkLb8vNvDdvnX0HA2nDq7p9V.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:764244'),
  ('976030993909730250', 'Lost Embrace', 2004, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Daniel Burman, Natalia Urruty, Ramiro Civita', 'Daniel Burman, Marcelo Birmajer', 'Daniel Hendler, Adriana Aizemberg, Jorge D''Elía, Sergio Boris, Melina Petriella, Rosita Londner, Diego Korol, Silvina Bosco', null, 'In Buenos Aires, the twenty-something Jewish-Argentinean Ariel Makaroff ditches the University of Architecture and spends his time wandering through the downtown gallery where his mother has a lingerie shop and his brother runs an importation business. Ariel has never understood why his father left him when he was a baby, but when his dad returns to Argentina, that will soon change.', 'In Buenos Aires, the twenty-something Jewish-Argentinean Ariel Makaroff ditches the University of Architecture and spends his time wandering through the downtown gallery where his mother has a lingerie shop and his brother runs an importation business. Ariel has never understood why his father left him when he was a baby, but when his dad returns to Argentina, that will soon change.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kmXuxzMazRbivZFLSg9kaOxNGCc.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:49681'),
  ('604369446472507730', 'Lost Flower: Eo Woo-dong', 2015, 'Drama, History, Thriller', 'Lee Soo-sung', 'Lee Soo-sung', 'Song Eun-Chae, Yeo Wook-hwan, Yoo Jang-young, Baek Do-bin, Kim Ki-doo, Nam Kyung-eup, Lee Bom, Yook Mi-ra', null, 'A triangular relationship between Eo Woo-dong, her husband Lee Dong, and fantasy character Moo-gong, highlights on the first half of the Joseon Dynasty and portrays the contradicted life of the high class people, criticizing the modern day Korean society.', 'A triangular relationship between Eo Woo-dong, her husband Lee Dong, and fantasy character Moo-gong, highlights on the first half of the Joseon Dynasty and portrays the contradicted life of the high class people, criticizing the modern day Korean society.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/5oUfcORCqjkDGAG9qMluqxcizi7.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:324671'),
