  ('876351611515269527', 'Louvre Come Back to Me!', 1962, 'Animation, Comedy', 'Chuck Jones, Maurice Noble', null, 'Mel Blanc, Julie Bennett', null, 'Pepe Le Pew, the eternally amorous skunk, is in Paris, where his stench sends a female cat upward to hit a freshly painted flagpole, which puts a white stripe on her back and causes Pepe to think she also is a skunk. He lustfully pursues her into the Louvre art gallery.', 'Pepe Le Pew, the eternally amorous skunk, is in Paris, where his stench sends a female cat upward to hit a freshly painted flagpole, which puts a white stripe on her back and causes Pepe to think she also is a skunk. He lustfully pursues her into the Louvre art gallery.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/8g01GVnvZ6Y1spsWBUnUsnptpKP.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:226822'),
  ('963828928184782675', 'Love', 1927, 'Drama, Romance', 'Edmund Goulding, John Gilbert, William H. Daniels', 'Ruth Cummings, Marian Ainslee, Frances Marion', 'John Gilbert, Greta Garbo, George Fawcett, Emily Fitzroy, Brandon Hurst, Philippe De Lacy, Mathilde Comont, Edward Connelly', 'NR', 'In Imperial Russia, Anna Karenina falls in love with the dashing military officer Count Vronsky and abandons her husband and child to become his mistress.', 'In Imperial Russia, Anna Karenina falls in love with the dashing military officer Count Vronsky and abandons her husband and child to become his mistress.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6Wdf0zB8DQeuquy5O3ldOK04Mfg.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:120831'),
